				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1733,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Implement VineHost trait for gRPC service\n\nImplement the `VineHost` trait for `MountainVinegRPCService` to bridge the generic `Vine` library with the Mountain backend. This enables the dedicated `Vine` crate to operate against Mountain's specific runtime—including its `AppHandle`-based event system—without requiring direct knowledge of Mountain's internal structure.\n\nThe implementation introduces `TauriRendererEmitter` to wrap Tauri's `Emitter` functionality and `InertIPCProvider` as a placeholder for non-reentrant notification handlers. This infrastructure supports the delegation of complex Cocoon → Mountain notification logic to the library level, facilitating the ongoing modularization of the backend.\n\nAdditionally, include the `Cache` crate in the workspace dependencies and update the Rust lints to recognize the `no_node_host` configuration flag.",
			"SHA": "2061488138b01ee892c438e7374e2e170b80650c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T12:43:19Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1732,
				32
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Delegate Vine notification logic to Vine crate\n\nFollowing the systematic modularization of the Mountain backend, replace the local gRPC notification handlers in `Source/Vine/Server/Notification/` with thin delegation shims pointing to the dedicated `Vine` crate.\n\nThis refactor extracts the implementation logic for all Cocoon → Mountain notifications—including complex batching and coalescing for `DecorationTypeLifecycle`, `OutputChannel`, and `ProgressReport`—into the `::Vine` library namespace. The Mountain-side modules are converted into thin wrappers that pass the `MountainVinegRPCService` and payload to the library implementation.\n\nThe `OutputChannelCoalesce::TryEnqueue` handler is updated to use the `TauriRendererEmitter` shim, allowing the library's coalescing logic to remain agnostic of the specific Tauri app handle while preserving the existing internal API surface.\n\nThis change enforces consistent IPC handling standards across the project and significantly reduces the code surface within the Mountain element.",
			"SHA": "452fafa5f558cfa180a348131f92caf25af1e508"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T12:42:41Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1732,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Delegate Vine connection logic to Vine crate\n\nFollowing the systematic modularization of the Mountain backend, replace the local gRPC connection logic for sidecars with a delegation to the dedicated `Vine` crate. The manual implementation in `TryConnectSingle.rs` is converted into a thin compatibility shim.\n\nThe refactor removes local handling of `tonic` channel configuration—including performance tuning for `LAND_TONIC_TUNED` and the optional `LAND_VINE_STREAMING` multiplexer initialization—in favor of the canonical `::Vine::Client::TryConnectSingle::Fn` implementation.\n\nThis ensures consistent gRPC client behavior and lifecycle management across the project while further reducing the internal code surface of the Mountain element.",
			"SHA": "9841398a265623f4879dfb0a08a1d1b86388d925"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T12:41:34Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1732,
				16
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Prune redundant Cache delegation modules\n\nFollowing the migration of caching logic to the central Cache crate, remove the intermediate module files for AssetMemoryMap and PathCanon that no longer have direct callers within the Mountain element.\n\nOnly the primary entry points—LoadOrInsert for asset mapping and Canonicalize for path security—are retained as local compatibility shims. This cleanup reduces the internal code surface of the Mountain element and enforces the use of the canonical ::Cache namespace for all other caching operations, such as statistics and cache invalidation.",
			"SHA": "159d9faaaed88c1b964443837baefdb822b6cb9a"
		}
	],
